  "facts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Szczecin, once the capital of the Duchy of Pomerania, was ruled by the Griffin dynasty and is now the largest city in Western Pomerania.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitszczecin.eu/en/history-szczecin",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Historically, Szczecin was known by several names—Sasin, Sedinum, Stetinum, and Stettin—reflecting its layered past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitszczecin.eu/en/history-szczecin",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The city’s industrial boom in the 19th century saw the rise of the Vulcan shipyard, a power station, and the Stoewer automobile factory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitszczecin.eu/en/history-szczecin",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the first half of the 19th century, military leaders began to consider removing Szczecin’s fortress status, signaling a shift toward civilian growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitszczecin.eu/en/history-szczecin",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Szczecin’s bourgeois elite hosted art salons, and scientific societies helped uncover Pomerania’s history, leading to the creation of the city museum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitszczecin.eu/en/history-szczecin",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The 1998 Polish local government reforms reduced the number of voivodeships to sixteen, but Szczecin remains the capital of the West Pomeranian Voivodeship.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
